The Audio module embeds an HTML5 audio player with optional cover art, title, and artist metadata. It supports common formats (MP3, OGG, WAV) by accepting file uploads from the Media Library or external URLs.

**Use Cases:**
*   Podcast episodes on show notes pages.
*   Music portfolios/showcasing original compositions.
*   Guided meditations or course audio alongside written content.

**Implementation:**
1.  Add the module via the Visual Builder (search for 'Audio').
2.  The settings are divided into three tabs: Content, Design, and Advanced.

**Content Tab Settings:**
*   `Text`: Enter track title/artist or description.
*   `Audio`: Select/upload audio file (MP3, OGG, WAV) or paste external URL.
*   `Image`: Upload cover art (album art, podcast artwork).
*   `Link`: Optionally wrap the module in a link.
*   `Background`: Apply background color, gradient, image, or video.
*   `Loop`: Enables repetition in loop-based layouts.
*   `Order`: Controls display order in dynamic contexts.
*   `Meta`: Sets an internal admin label for identification.

**Design Tab Settings:**
Controls visual styling for the player and surrounding elements. Options include: Image styling, Caption Text styling, Title Text styling, Sizing, Spacing, Border, Box Shadow, Filters, Transform, and Animation. These settings utilize shared options groups (e.g., [Text], [Title Text], [Sizing]).

**Advanced Tab Settings:**
Provides developer-oriented controls for custom attributes, conditional display, and interactions.
*   `Attributes`: Assign CSS ID, reusable classes, or custom HTML attributes.
*   `CSS`: Add custom CSS code to fine-tune the module.
*   `Conditions`: Display rules (user role, page type, date, logic).
*   `Visibility`: Device visibility toggles.
*   `Transitions`: Controls animation timing.
*   `Position`: Precise placement control.
*   `Scroll Effects`: Control behavior during scrolling.

