The Icon List module generates visually engaging lists where each item contains a title, an icon (from the Divi library or uploaded), and optional descriptive body text. It supports both Block mode (vertical stacking) and Flex mode (horizontal wrapping). Items can be managed via add/edit/remove interfaces, with individual settings allowing per-item overrides for icon size, color, and text styling. The module structure includes: 

**Content Tab:** Controls list items (add/edit/reorder), link behavior (making the entire module clickable), background application, loop builder enablement, display order (`number`), and admin label (`admin label`).

**Individual Item Settings:** Allows setting `Title` (text), optional `Body` (rich text), selecting an `Icon` (icon picker/upload), and applying specific `Design Overrides` for the item.

**Design Tab:** Controls overall styling, including choosing the `Layout` (dropdown: Block or Flex) and configuring default icon size, color, and appearance. Shared design options are available via Options Groups like Text, Body Text, Spacing, etc.

**Technical Details:**
*   **Block Identifier:** `divi/icon-list`
*   **CSS Selectors (Example):** 
    ```css
    /* Style the Icon List container */
    .et_pb_icon_list {
        list-style: none;
        padding: 0;
    }
    /* Style individual list items */
    .et_pb_icon_list .et_pb_icon_list_item {
        display: flex;
        align-items: flex-start;
        gap: 16px;
        padding: 12px 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #eeeeee;
    }
    .et_pb_icon_list .et_pb_icon_list_item:last-child {
        border-bottom: none;
    }
    /* Icon circle background */
    .et_pb_icon_list .et_pb_icon_list_icon {
        background: #f0f4ff;
        border-radius: 50%;
        padding: 12px;
        flex-shrink: 0;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
    }
    /* Hover effect on items */
    .et_pb_icon_list .et_pb_icon_list_item:hover {
        background: #f9f9f9;
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding-left: 12px;
        transition: all 0.3s ease;
    }
    /* Responsive adjustments */
    @media (max-width: 767px) {
        .et_pb_icon_list .et_pb_icon_list_item {
            gap: 12px;
        }
    }
    ```
*   **REST API Interaction:** 
    *   Reading content uses a brace-depth parser on `post_content` block JSON.
    *   Modifying existing modules uses `wp.apiFetch` PATCH on the post endpoint to update attributes in `post_content`.
    *   Creating new modules requires browser automation (e.g., Playwright) because REST creation may not render correctly in the Visual Builder layer view.

**Use Cases:** 
*   Feature highlights/checklists (using checkmark/X icons for inclusion/exclusion).
*   Step-by-step process guides or workflows.
*   Contact information blocks (e.g., phone, email, address) with click-to-contact links (`tel:`, `mailto:`).

**Limitations:** 
*   Do not use Icon List for a single standalone icon (use [Icon] module).
*   Do not use Icon List for long descriptions in a card layout (use [Blurb] modules in columns).
*   Do not use Icon List for simple bullet or numbered lists (use [Text] module with HTML list markup).

