.et_pb_search .et_pb_s {
    background-color: #f5f5f5;
    border: 2px solid #ddd;
    border-radius: 25px;
    padding: 12px 20px;
    font-size: 16px;
    transition: border-color 0.3s ease;
}

/* Highlight the input field on focus */
.et_pb_search .et_pb_s:focus {
    border-color: #2ea3f2;
    outline: none;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(46, 163, 242, 0.15);
}

/* Style the search button */
.et_pb_search .et_pb_searchsubmit {
    background-color: #2ea3f2;
    border-radius: 0 25px 25px 0;
    padding: 12px 24px;
    font-weight: 600;
}

/* Responsive: full-width search on mobile */
@media (max-width: 767px) {
    .et_pb_search {
        width: 100%;
    }
    .et_pb_search .et_pb_s {
        font-size: 14px;
    }
}
```]

The Shop module integrates Divi's Visual Builder with WooCommerce, allowing product display anywhere without relying on default WooCommerce templates. It pulls data (featured image, title, price, rating, add-to-cart button) from the WC catalog and renders it in a styled grid.

**Usage:** Ideal for homepage featured sections, category landing pages, or dedicated sale/clearance areas. Do not use it on product page templates; use individual Woo Product modules instead.

**Availability:** Requires WooCommerce to be installed and activated. The module is available once WC is running and at least one product is published.

**Block Identifier:** `divi/shop`

**Key Settings (Content Tab):**
*   **Type:** Selects the product query type: Recent, Featured, Sale, Best Selling, or Top Rated Products.
*   **Posts Number:** Sets the maximum number of products to display.
*   **Include Categories:** Filters products by one or more WC categories.
*   **Columns:** Sets the grid column count (1–6).
*   **Orderby/Order:** Controls product sorting (e.g., Date, Title, Price, Popularity, Rating; Ascending/Descending).
*   **Elements Toggles:** Control visibility of title, price, rating, add-to-cart button, and sale badge.
